"""Fixtures for the Go gateway's read API (A-9 S6), generated by driving the Python read API (read_api.py: create_api_app, Access,
Viewer) through Starlette's test client over a seeded store, as a set of callers.

The seeded store (FakeStore below) follows PgReadStore's SQL clause by clause over the same rows the Go test inserts into a
scratch Postgres: sessions, results, human requests, events, holds and the pinned-definition rows. The callers are an auditor
(admin), a session's own person, a member of a team that owns an agent, a person of an unrelated team, an unauthenticated and a
bad-token caller, a workload, a delegate acting for each of those people (and for a malformed person), a delegate acting for
nobody, and a notifier. Each case is one request: the method, path, the caller (token and X-Hangar-On-Behalf-Of) and what
Python answered: the status, the content type, Allow, and the exact JSON body.

A case may carry "go": the expectation for Go where it deliberately differs from Python, with "why". The Go test fails on a "go"
without a "why" and on a "why" without a "go".

The metrics fixture (gateway/internal/metrics/testdata/metrics.json) is the exposition metrics.TriggerMetrics renders after a
script of calls; the OTLP one (gateway/internal/otlplogs/testdata/otlp.json) is the request otlp_logs.OTLPLogHandler posts for a
script of records. Called by tools/gen_gateway_registry.py (outputs()).
"""
